Vital OS 0.1.0
================

Original Vital OS branding (mark, wordmark, wallpapers, Plymouth theme,
GRUB theme, GNOME Shell stylesheet, Vital Welcome, and Vital Marketplace)
is released under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or later.

Third-party components installed by the image build, not vendored as
binaries in this repository except the Flathub remote description:

- Ubuntu 24.04 LTS packages, various licenses. Ubuntu is a trademark of
  Canonical Ltd. Vital OS is not a Canonical product.
- Inter and IBM Plex, SIL Open Font License, via fonts-inter and
  fonts-ibm-plex.
- Papirus icon theme, GPL-3.0, via papirus-icon-theme.
- papirus-folders 1.14.0, MIT, used only at build time to tint folders.
- Dash to Dock 100, GPL-2.0, installed from the upstream release archive.
- Desktop Icons NG, GPL-3.0, via gnome-shell-extension-desktop-icons-ng.
- Firefox, Mozilla Public License, from packages.mozilla.org.
- Calamares, GPL-3.0.
- GNOME, Adwaita, and other desktop components, their respective licenses.

Vital OS can send an anonymous install count: a random id, the OS version,
and a weekly check-in. It does not send a name, username, email, hostname,
or hardware id. The switch is in Vital Welcome. See
/usr/share/vitalos/PRIVACY.md. Ubuntu's Settings package depends on
whoopsie-preferences; the whoopsie service is masked in this image.
Applications you install later may have their own update checks.
